 "answer": "Apple's revenue rose through the 2025 holiday quarter, then eased in 2026. Here are the last five reported quarters (fiscal quarters, USD):\n\n| Period (end date) | Revenue | Form, filed | Accession no. |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Q2 FY25 (Jun 28, 2025) | $94.04B | 10-Q, 2026-07-31 | 0000320193-26-000020 |\n| Q3 FY25 (Sep 27, 2025) | $102.47B (derived) | 10-K, 2025-10-31 | 0000320193-25-000079 |\n| Q4 FY25 (Dec 27, 2025) | $143.76B | 10-Q, 2026-01-30 | 0000320193-26-000006 |\n| Q1 FY26 (Mar 28, 2026) | $111.18B | 10-Q, 2026-05-01 | 0000320193-26-000013 |\n| Q2 FY26 (Jun 27, 2026) | $109.42B | 10-Q, 2026-07-31 | 0000320193-26-000020 |\n\nXBRL tag for all rows: us-gaap:RevenueFromContractWithCustomerExcludingAssessedTax.\n\n**Trend:**\n- Revenue climbed from $94.04B to $102.47B over the first two quarters shown.\n- The December quarter was the peak at $143.76B, which is the seasonal holiday high.\n- It then fell to $111.18B in the March quarter and $109.42B in the June quarter.\n- The June 2026 quarter was up about 16% from the June 2025 quarter ($109.42B vs. $94.04B).\n\nThe Q3 FY25 figure is derived rather than directly reported, so treat it as slightly less certain.\n\nFreshness: latest filing used was filed 2026-07-31; data as of 2026-10-18T20:34:06Z.",
